[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mSeal Guest Backed Session Drivers For The Creator Platform\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Port provides a real provider-backed hosted execution lane for `cloud-aws` on prepared AWS x86_64 PVM hosts as the substrate for creator-platform guest sessions. (\u001b[2minspect verified hosted AWS PVM mission VFgcM1Zpu and epic VFgcPDfEj\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - `port control-plane prepare-pvm-node`, `port machine launch --machine cloud-aws`, `port machine status --machine cloud-aws`, and `port machine stop --machine cloud-aws` succeed through the hosted control-plane and node-agent path for the canonical AWS lane. (\u001b[2minspect verified hosted AWS PVM mission VFgcM1Zpu and epic VFgcPDfEj\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - Port exposes stable guest-session identity and driver metadata for guest-backed shell flows so upstream systems can treat Port sessions as one audited shell driver. (\u001b[2mVFgtgGEog\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-04\u001b[0m - Guest-backed `pty`, `exec`, and `forward` behavior remains canonical and consumable by higher-level product surfaces without inventing a second shell protocol. (\u001b[2mVFgtgGWoh\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-05\u001b[0m - Failure surfaces stay explicit: missing host kit, missing artifacts, wrong lane, or unstable guest-session metadata fail honestly without silent fallback. (\u001b[2minspect canonical failure paths plus automated tests\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (2):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFgtgGWoh\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Shell Driver Integration Contract For Upstream Control Planes (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFgtgGEog\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Guest Session Identity And Audit Surface (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-04-02T19:31:48\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFgtZtnzb/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Seal Guest Backed Session Drivers For The Creator Platform - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Port provides a real provider-backed hosted execution lane for `cloud-aws` on prepared AWS x86_64 PVM hosts as the substrate for creator-platform guest sessions. | manual: inspect verified hosted AWS PVM mission VFgcM1Zpu and epic VFgcPDfEj |\r\n| MG-02 | `port control-plane prepare-pvm-node`, `port machine launch --machine cloud-aws`, `port machine status --machine cloud-aws`, and `port machine stop --machine cloud-aws` succeed through the hosted control-plane and node-agent path for the canonical AWS lane. | manual: inspect verified hosted AWS PVM mission VFgcM1Zpu and epic VFgcPDfEj |\r\n| MG-03 | Port exposes stable guest-session identity and driver metadata for guest-backed shell flows so upstream systems can treat Port sessions as one audited shell driver. | board: VFgtgGEog |\r\n| MG-04 | Guest-backed `pty`, `exec`, and `forward` behavior remains canonical and consumable by higher-level product surfaces without inventing a second shell protocol. | board: VFgtgGWoh |\r\n| MG-05 | Failure surfaces stay explicit: missing host kit, missing artifacts, wrong lane, or unstable guest-session metadata fail honestly without silent fallback. | manual: inspect canonical failure paths plus automated tests |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Scope is AWS x86_64 hosted PVM first.\r\n- Keep the existing Port verb model.\r\n- Do not move creator-facing policy or domain/auth concerns into Port.\r\n- Reuse the verified hosted AWS PVM runtime contract as the substrate baseline; do not fork or duplicate it as a second runtime lane.\r\n- Keep guest-backed shell behavior on the existing Port guest protocol surface rather than inventing a creator-specific shell protocol.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while creator-platform guest sessions still depend on ad hoc session identifiers, unstable driver labels, or a creator-specific shell protocol on `cloud-aws`.\r\n- HALT when the verified AWS hosted PVM runtime contract plus the attached epics prove one audited Port shell-driver surface for guest-backed `exec`, `pty`, and `forward`, with explicit failure guidance.\r\n- YIELD if the remaining blocker is a product decision about creator-facing identity policy, audit retention semantics, or auth/domain ownership outside Port.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFgtgGEog\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mGuest Session Identity And Audit Surface\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 19:26:12\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 19:50:31\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 20:03:37\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-02 20:03:37\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m13m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgtgGEog/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgtgGEog/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port can already broker guest-backed shell flows, but upstream creator systems still lack a stable Port-owned session identity and driver metadata surface for treating those flows as one audited shell driver across hosted AWS PVM execution.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Surface a stable Port-owned guest-session identity for creator-facing shell flows. (Upstream systems can resolve one durable Port session identifier across hosted guest \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mexec\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpty\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mforward\u001b[0m workflows. -> One canonical guest-session identity contract with proof coverage)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Expose driver metadata that lets upstream systems classify Port as one audited shell driver. (Port surfaces one driver identity/metadata shape rather than per-verb ad hoc labels. -> One canonical driver metadata contract used across guest-backed shell flows)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Keep the audit boundary inside Port without absorbing creator policy or auth concerns. (The surfaced metadata is runtime/driver scoped and excludes creator-domain policy fields. -> One explicit boundary in docs and automated coverage)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must emit a stable guest-session identity for guest-backed hosted shell workflows so one launched session can be correlated across \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mexec\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpty\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mforward\u001b[0m operations.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must surface driver metadata that identifies the session as one Port-owned audited shell driver rather than a set of unrelated per-verb transports.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Session identity and driver metadata must be exposed through canonical Port surfaces rather than a parallel creator-specific API.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Missing, stale, or unsupported session metadata must fail with explicit guidance and no silent fallback to anonymous or ambiguous session state.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Session identity and driver metadata must remain stable across repeated guest-backed operations for the same underlying hosted AWS PVM session.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Verification must include focused automated coverage plus at least one human-reviewable proof surface showing the metadata contract.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Boundary control: Planning and docs review with targeted tests\r\n    - Driver metadata: CLI or protocol proof plus docs review\r\n    - Session identity: Focused automated tests across guest-backed hosted flows\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 0 | manual 12\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 0 | manual 6\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 6 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bd7U\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Guest Session Identity Contract (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
[5.4, "o", "$ keel epic show VFgtgGWoh\r\n"]
[5.85, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mShell Driver Integration Contract For Upstream Control Planes\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 19:26:12\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 20:04:05\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 20:12:08\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-02 20:12:08\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m8m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgtgGWoh/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgtgGWoh/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port exposes canonical guest exec, pty, and forward verbs, but upstream control planes still need a sealed integration contract that proves those guest-backed flows remain consumable as one shell driver without inventing a second shell protocol or hiding runtime failures.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Seal one upstream integration contract for guest-backed shell behavior on Port. (Upstream systems can consume guest \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mexec\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpty\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mforward\u001b[0m as one Port shell driver contract. -> One canonical integration contract and proof path)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Preserve the existing Port guest protocol and verb model as the canonical transport surface. (No new creator-specific shell protocol is required for upstream integration. -> One contract that reuses existing Port verbs and protocol frames)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Keep provider and runtime failures explicit for higher-level product surfaces. (Wrong lane, missing host kit, and missing artifacts surface actionable errors without fallback. -> One documented and tested failure contract for upstream control planes)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must define one canonical upstream shell-driver contract for guest-backed \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mexec\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpty\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mforward\u001b[0m on the hosted AWS PVM lane.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - The integration contract must preserve the existing Port guest protocol frames and verb model rather than inventing a second creator-specific shell protocol.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must document and verify the lifecycle semantics that upstream systems can rely on for streamed PTY/forward and command-style exec behavior.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Wrong lane, missing host kit, missing artifacts, or unsupported hosted prerequisites must fail with actionable guidance and no silent fallback.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The contract must remain consumable through the canonical Port CLI/runtime surfaces so local and hosted behavior stay comparable.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Verification must cover both successful guest-backed shell flows and explicit provider-aware failure surfaces.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgu7Bp7V\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strateg